# CDK Data & Messaging Resources

## DynamoDB

- **Table:** Partition key (PK), sort key (SK); billing PAY_PER_REQUEST; stream NEW_AND_OLD_IMAGES if using Streams; pointInTimeRecovery; removalPolicy RETAIN for prod
- **GSI:** Add GSIs for access patterns (e.g. GSI1PK/GSI1SK); projection ALL or specific attributes
- **Idempotency table:** Separate table or dedicated PK prefix; TTL attribute for expiry; grant Lambda read/write

## SQS

- **Queue:** Standard or FIFO; visibility timeout ≥ 6× Lambda timeout for batch; dead-letter queue after max receives; redrive allow policy on DLQ source
- **Event source mapping:** Lambda event source for queue; batch size (e.g. 10); optional filter
- **Retry ladder:** Primary → DLQ; consumer of DLQ can have different handler or alert

## SNS

- **Topic:** Standard or FIFO; FIFO requires content-based dedup or message group ID
- **Subscription:** SqsSubscription to queue; filter policy for message attributes; raw message delivery if needed
- **Fan-out:** Multiple queues subscribe to same topic; filter per subscriber if needed

## DynamoDB Streams

- **Stream:** Enable on table (NEW_AND_OLD_IMAGES or NEW_IMAGE); Lambda event source mapping to stream; batch size and bisect on error for partial failure
- **IAM:** Lambda needs dynamodb:GetRecords, GetShardIterator, ListStreams, and stream ARN resource

## RDS Proxy

- **Proxy:** Create RDS Proxy in front of RDS cluster; Lambda in VPC uses proxy endpoint; secrets for DB credentials in Secrets Manager
- **Grant:** Lambda role needs rds-db:connect and access to secret

## Conventions

- Least privilege IAM; pass resource ARNs/names to Lambda via env; use constructs for reuse

## Anti-Patterns

- No DLQ for queues; visibility timeout too short; no stream on table when using Streams; broad IAM

